      <dico>Lessing</dico>
      <unicode>ᠰᠠᠴᠠ</unicode>
      <uighur>saCa</uighur>
      <transcript>SACA</transcript>
      <definition>[= saca, caca; T, tsha tsha, s, saccha= sac-chāye ?.] n. Small, often cone-shaped objects representing miniature pagodas (S. stupas) or deities used variously in Buddhist cult. They are usually kneaded of clay, sometimes with the admixture of the ashes of a lama. See G. Tucci, Indo-Tibetica, I, p. 53 ff (Rome, 1932).</definition>
      <page>654</page>
    </entry_item>
